{"activity_text": "Anti-Gram+, Anticancer", "article_id": "", "assay_text": "Unknown", "assay_type": "", "comments_text": "Sequence analysis: APD analysis reveals that this sequence is similar (95.83%) to Brevinin-1GHd L=F=S: 13%, A=K: 17%. GRAVY: 1.0375, mol wt: 2527.141; mol formula: C119H194N28O28S2; mol ex coeff: 0. Chemical modification: one S-S bond for the Rana box. Activity: active against S. aureus (MIC 1.5 uM), B-subtilis (MIC>24.8 uM), E-coli (MIC>24.8 uM), A-baumanii (MIC>24.8 uM), K-pneumonia (MIC>24.8 uM), and P-aeruginosa (MIC>24.8 uM). Cancer cells: inhibit the proliferation of A549 lung (IC50 31.6 uM), AGS stomach (IC50 7.5 uM), Jurkat blood (IC50 12.9 uM,) HCT116 colon (IC50 9.2 uM), HL60 blood (IC50 14.8 uM), and HepG2 liver (IC50 11.7 uM). In vitro toxicity: human RBC: HC50= 41.87 uM, less hemo.lytic.", "concentration": "", "cytotoxicity_text": "", "hemolytic_activity_text": "", "measure_group": "", "measure_value": "", "pubmed_id": "40864826", "record_granularity": "entry_text", "reference_text": "Curr Issues Mol Biol. 2025 Aug 20;47(8):673. doi: 10.3390/cimb47080673. PubMed", "sequence_key": "APD6:AP05672", "source_id": "AP05672", "source_numeric_id": "05672", "source_path": "APD6/apd6_export/structured/peptides.csv", "source_record_id": "AP05672", "source_table": "peptides.csv", "stability_text": "", "subject_name": "", "target_organism_text": "", "title": "Cloning and Functional Characterization of a Novel Brevinin-1-Type Peptide from Sylvirana guentheri with Anticancer Activity.", "unit": "", "﻿database": "APD6"}
